{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ncfg=json.load(open('update42.json'))['interpretations'][0]   # current config account (8d521d6e)\ncfg=json.loads(json.dumps(cfg))\n# correct the knowledge use in the interpretation\nfor k in cfg['knowledge']:\n    if k['entry_id']=='98ee8dfd5fac4b84915f91ed4b094bcf-knowledge-2':\n        k['revision']=2\n        k['assertion']=\\\"The tracked configuration is written from log entries by processConfigurationLogEntry (called by appendEntries for new entries and by the startup scan), by appendConfigurationEntry on the leader, by the conflict rollback in appendEntries, and independently from snapshot metadata by restoreSnapshot and installSnapshot; the FSM's ConfigurationStore is never read back.\\\"\nnote=(\\\"Correction note: an earlier statement in this account described processConfigurationLogEntry as the only writer of the tracked configuration state, which is too strong - restoreSnapshot installs the newest local snapshot's committed configuration (api.go:677-678), installSnapshot installs the metadata of a streamed snapshot (raft.go:1960-1961), appendConfigurationEntry records the configuration it appends on the leader (raft.go:1238), and the conflict path in appendEntries rolls the latest configuration back to the committed one (raft.go:1548) - while processConfigurationLogEntry remains the writer for entries taken from the log, called from appendEntries and from the startup scan. The mechanism the account relies on is unchanged and in fact sharpened: the startup inputs are the snapshot's configuration and the log scan, and the scan's lower bound is what the feature moves. \\\")\ncfg['rationale']=note+cfg['rationale']\ncorr={\\\"id\\\":\\\"98ee8dfd5fac4b84915f91ed4b094bcf-knowledge-2\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"changed_premise\\\":\\\"The earlier statement restricted the writers of the tracked configuration to processConfigurationLogEntry for log entries, which understates the sources: the snapshot paths and the leader's own configuration append also write it, so the tracked state can be established without any configuration entry being processed.\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":\\\"The tracked configuration state has several writers: processConfigurationLogEntry for LogConfiguration and deprecated peer entries taken from the log (called by appendEntries for newly appended entries and by the NewRaft startup scan), appendConfigurationEntry on the leader for the configuration it appends, the conflict path in appendEntries which rolls latest back to committed when a suffix is deleted below the latest configuration index, restoreSnapshot for the newest local snapshot's committed configuration, and installSnapshot for the metadata of a snapshot received from a leader. The FSM's ConfigurationStore is never read back into that state.\\\",\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Applies to every node; the snapshot writers matter at startup and during a streamed install, the log writer while entries arrive, and the FSM-side store is write-only from raft's perspective (api.go:677-678, raft.go:1238, 1548, 1595-1620, 1960-1961).\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_process_config_entry\\\",\\\"src_restore_snapshot_config\\\",\\\"src_newraft_startup\\\",\\\"src_restore_committed\\\"],\n \\\"affected_uses\\\":[\\\"8d521d6ed34941308ba2f976b1f41dc6-interpretation-0\\\",\\\"d958d473b5d74a9a83c0de5b55a64ce5-interpretation-0\\\"]}\njson.dump({\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Corrects an over-strong statement about the writers of raft's tracked configuration, in the knowledge record and in the configuration-recovery account that relied on it; the mechanism the account uses is unchanged and in fact sharpened by the enumeration.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[corr],\\\"interpretations\\\":[cfg]},open('update43.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update43.json 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"\nimport sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint('valid',d['valid'],'no_change',d.get('no_change'))\nfor x in d.get('diagnostics',[])[:8]: print(x['paths'],x['message'])\nprint([(e['object'],e['action'],e.get('target')) for e in d.get('effects',[])])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
